# A tenant: a Trusted Domain built from its written spec to a verified
# cluster (docs/stratus.adoc, D14).
#
# The size is the spec's, written before this plays by `domain new` (or the
# controller's SIZE and COMMIT, which send that line and then this play).
# This file is the procedure, never the shape: spec.yaml stays the truth of
# what a domain is.
#
# The build asks before the first step that bills. A NO there, or Ctrl-C,
# leaves the build where it stands, and the play stops at the claim that the
# cluster is installed; `play ~/tenant.mise --param NAME=…` again goes on
# from the first step not done.
@name         tenant
@description  Build a Trusted Domain from its spec through the cluster's install, verify it, and answer its status.
@param        NAME
@answers      TENANT

# Only a domain built here is built on; an adopted one is planned against.
expect domain ${NAME} class eq built
domain build ${NAME} --through run
expect domain ${NAME} step run eq done

# Ten checks against the cluster through its kubeconfig, which stays on the
# host; the block-volume probe is one of them, so this needs the tasks tier,
# as the build did.
domain verify ${NAME}
expect domain ${NAME} verify eq 10

TENANT=$(domain ${NAME})
